<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sophie of Bar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1018–<a href="/years/1093">1093</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sophie, Countess of Bar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sophie of Bar was countess of Bar from 1033, a descendant of Duke Frederick of Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lorraine">Lorraine</a>. Around 1038 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-of-mousson">Louis of Mousson</a>, count of Montbéliard. Their descendants ruled the county of Bar, later the duchy of Bar, as a separate principality between Champagne and Lorraine.</p></div>
